# Line endings.
#
# Shell scripts are COPYd into Linux images verbatim, and a CRLF shebang is
# "/usr/bin/env: bash\r: No such file or directory" -- the sandbox crash-loops
# at boot. Git on Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default, so any
# Windows contributor who rebuilds the image ships that crash unless these
# files are pinned to LF.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
sandbox/tools.conf text eol=lf
sandbox/supervisord.conf text eol=lf
sandbox/firefox-policies.json text eol=lf
sandbox/Dockerfile* text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
